/-! # Kerr–Newman BL: rational atoms and domains (ATLAS-IV-02)

Atoms (B3 class B notation wrappers): `Ui a r θ = 1/Σ` and `Wi θ = 1/sin θ` are reused unchanged from
`Atlas.Kerr.InAtoms` (same `Σ = r² + a² cos²θ`); `Di M a Q r = 1/Δ` is new. The derivative rules
below are the only analytic input of the generated tables.

Domains: `domReg M a Q = {Σ ≠ 0, Δ ≠ 0, sin θ ≠ 0}` (open, every real `M a Q`) and the target
`domKN M a Q = {r₊ < r, 0 < θ < π}`. On `domKN` with `0 < M`: `r > 0`, `Σ > 0`, `Δ > 0`,
`sin θ > 0`, hence `domKN ⊆ domReg`. Neither `a = 0` nor `Q = 0` is excluded; no point with
`Δ = 0` or `Σ = 0` lies in either set. -/

open Real

namespace ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.KN

open ExactVacuumAtlas.Kerr.In (Ui Wi)

/-! ## The regular set `domReg` -/

/-! ## The target domain `domKN` -/

theorem isOpen_domKN (M a Q : ℝ) : IsOpen (domKN M a Q) := by
  have h1 : IsOpen {x : Pt 4 | rPlus M a Q < x 1} := isOpen_lt continuous_const (continuous_apply 1)
  have h2 : IsOpen {x : Pt 4 | 0 < x 2} := isOpen_lt continuous_const (continuous_apply 2)
  have h3 : IsOpen {x : Pt 4 | x 2 < π} := isOpen_lt (continuous_apply 2) continuous_const
  have e : domKN M a Q = {x : Pt 4 | rPlus M a Q < x 1} ∩ ({x : Pt 4 | 0 < x 2} ∩ {x : Pt 4 | x 2 < π}) := by
    ext x; simp [domKN]
  rw [e]; exact h1.inter (h2.inter h3)

end ExactVacuumAtlas.EinsteinMaxwell.KN
end R05Seg2

